caelum (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 1.3.0.
    - Opaque sky (on by default): Caelum paints the whole sky, so the
      wallpaper no longer changes its colours; the exported wallpaper and
      lock screen get a real daytime sky.
    - Click-through: clicks on the sky reach the desktop; only the gear,
      compass and forecast cards respond. Clicking the compass or a card
      starts explore mode with constellation names on hover.
    - Weather refreshed right after suspend or hibernation, with retries
      while the network comes back.
    - Version shown in Settings; new caelum --version option.
    - New screenshots.

 -- Juliowilly <jw.adamagaba@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:02:21 +0000

caelum (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 1.2.0.
    - Sun and moon hidden only by clouds actually in front of them; thin
      cirrus no longer veils the sun.
    - Low clouds drawn in perspective across the whole sky, drifting with
      the wind; overcast deck and altostratus sheet.
    - Planets fade in with twilight instead of showing in daylight.
    - Cloud layer cached at half resolution: much lower CPU use.
    - New screenshots.

 -- Juliowilly <jw.adamagaba@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:32:27 +0000

